  "prediction": "**Implementing Telework to Reduce Office Space: Challenges and Opportunities**\n\nThe Government Accountability Office (GAO) conducted a study to examine how civilian Chief Financial Officer (CFO) Act agencies use telework to reduce office space and improve space efficiency. The study found that 23 civilian CFO Act agencies reported using telework to reduce space, with 15 agencies incorporating telework into their space planning policies.\n\nThe study identified three scenarios for using telework to reduce space: (1) limited telework with no space reduction, (2) moderate telework with some space reduction, and (3) extensive telework with significant space reduction. The General Services Administration (GSA) defines mobility as an overarching strategy that includes telework, hoteling, and other space-saving initiatives.\n\nThe study found that agencies face challenges in using telework to reduce space, including human capital issues, such as negotiating with unions and managing employee expectations. Agencies also struggle to measure the cost-effectiveness of telework and space reduction initiatives.\n\nThe study highlighted the success of the General Services Administration (GSA) in leveraging telework to reduce space. GSA has implemented a comprehensive mobility strategy that includes telework, hoteling, and other space-saving initiatives. GSA's efforts have resulted in significant space reductions, with some agencies achieving up to 30% reductions in office space.\n\nThe study made two recommendations to the GSA: (1) develop guidance on using telework as a strategic space-saving tool, and (2) complete the Workplace Investment and Feasibility Tool to help agencies assess the cost-effectiveness of telework and space reduction initiatives.\n\nOverall, the study suggests that telework can be a valuable tool for reducing office space and improving space efficiency, but agencies face significant challenges in implementing these initiatives. With the right guidance and tools, agencies can leverage telework to achieve significant space reductions and improve their overall space efficiency.",
